    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pick\n\n### Question\n\nI use a lot the buffer picker and I noticed some inconsistencies :   \r\nwhen I open files with mini.files or mini.pick (files), it shows the relative path but when I open another one with \"LSP Go To definition\" (eg. mini.pick through mini.extra), it is opened with the absolute filepath.\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7fcd4968-3242-4625-b974-0a90df714847)\r\n\r\n\r\nIs there a way to overwrite the picker to display only the relative path to the current working directory (cwd) and improve the readability?\r\nThanks!",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.pick</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I use a lot the buffer picker and I noticed some inconsistencies :<br>\nwhen I open files with mini.files or mini.pick (files), it shows the relative path but when I open another one with \"LSP Go To definition\" (eg. mini.pick through mini.extra), it is opened with the absolute filepath.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/34398/400255158-7fcd4968-3242-4625-b974-0a90df714847.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..oGrgh3zahT0A1I4VMJjOm9t9WKtzpXyIXENHmxS8sjA\"><img src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/34398/400255158-7fcd4968-3242-4625-b974-0a90df714847.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..oGrgh3zahT0A1I4VMJjOm9t9WKtzpXyIXENHmxS8sjA\" alt=\"image\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"></a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Is there a way to overwrite the picker to display only the relative path to the current working directory (cwd) and improve the readability?<br>\nThanks!</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.pick\nQuestion\nI use a lot the buffer picker and I noticed some inconsistencies :\nwhen I open files with mini.files or mini.pick (files), it shows the relative path but when I open another one with \"LSP Go To definition\" (eg. mini.pick through mini.extra), it is opened with the absolute filepath.\n\nIs there a way to overwrite the picker to display only the relative path to the current working directory (cwd) and improve the readability?\nThanks!",
