                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "Thanks for the repro steps!\r\n\r\n> If I run again `:cd c:\\CODE\\gomini`, it displays the relative path :\r\n\r\nI indeed can reproduce and this was the main clue to this: I have [auto root set up](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/b1af49d98233180c6045e81f4aef5b663d032b62/doc/mini-misc.txt#L124) which seems to act as that manual `:cd` step.\r\n\r\nThe thing is, 'mini.pick' already should open any file with relative path, but it doesn't do that here for some reason. I'll take a look.\r\n",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Thanks for the repro steps!</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">If I run again <code class=\"notranslate\">:cd c:\\CODE\\gomini</code>, it displays the relative path :</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I indeed can reproduce and this was the main clue to this: I have <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/b1af49d98233180c6045e81f4aef5b663d032b62/doc/mini-misc.txt#L124\">auto root set up</a> which seems to act as that manual <code class=\"notranslate\">:cd</code> step.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The thing is, 'mini.pick' already should open any file with relative path, but it doesn't do that here for some reason. I'll take a look.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "Thanks for the repro steps!\n\nIf I run again :cd c:\\CODE\\gomini, it displays the relative path :\n\nI indeed can reproduce and this was the main clue to this: I have auto root set up which seems to act as that manual :cd step.\nThe thing is, 'mini.pick' already should open any file with relative path, but it doesn't do that here for some reason. I'll take a look.",
